  action: ANNOTATED
  changes: 'Edison LITERATURE (PaperQA3) identity research; report at research/ingredients/Iron_as_FeCl3_in_EDTA-edison-literature.md
    (local artifact — research/ is gitignored, so the findings are quoted here rather
    than linked). Report verdict: **Recommended interpretation:** an **underspecified
    iron-chelate preparation/formulation**, not a uniquely identified single chemical.
    The wording says that iron is supplied from ferric chloride in the presence of
    EDTA. A published experimental preparation called “ferric EDTA” was made by mixing
    ferric chloride and disodium EDTA at a 1:1 Fe:EDTA molar ratio, supporting formation
    of a ferric–EDTA c CURIEs discussed: NCIT:C598. Recorded as provenance only —
    no grounding applied from this run. Edison''s recommendations are deliberately
    conservative, and a plausible identifier promoted by a mechanism that never decided
    anything is what #203 and #263 exist to undo. Any CURIE above is a curator''s
    to accept or reject.'
